Z||000015||BRIAN CORNELIUS||07-02-2001||06:22 PM||||A clarification about the size. After I have saved the image and print it the size of the square area the face is on is 6.4 by 6.7 inches or about 30% too large! What process should I use to reduce it to the correct size?||||reg||5
Z||000016||AusFiero||07-02-2001||07:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BRIAN CORNELIUS:<BR><B>A clarification about the size. After I have saved the image and print it the size of the square area the face is on is 6.4 by 6.7 inches or about 30% too large! What process should I use to reduce it to the correct size?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I am assuming you have you printer set at the wrong resolution? you will need to set it at 150DPI. 30% bigger would mean about 200DPI, which is a common faxing resolution. I have 300DPI Versions of the images but at 97 meg a set, they won't be going online<BR>||||reg||1
