Z||000021||BRIAN CORNELIUS||07-03-2001||11:03 AM||||I checked for resolution setting, but do not have any specific readings ( I have a HP Deskjet 722c). The display when I select print preview is width of 6.4" and Height of 6.6". I can change these numbers. What should I use to get the proper size when I print the faces? ||||reg||1
Z||000022||DecadenceR||07-03-2001||11:24 AM||||Brian, I have a 660C. I dont know if the settings are the same, but try this....<BR>Go to flie, then print setup. A box should pop up with your settings. Click on Properties next to your printer name. Then on the top there, click the Graphics tab. It shoudl say Resolution and there should be a drop box with the different printing resolutions. Just click on 150 and click OK. Good luck.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SigPic.jpg"> <BR>AIM - DecadenceR||||reg||1
